  "_skill_md": "---\nname: linkedin\ndescription: Internal API for linkedin\nmetadata:\n  author: unbrowse\n  version: \"1.0\"\n  baseUrl: \"https://www.linkedin.com\"\n  authMethod: \"Session Token (csrf-token)\"\n  endpointCount: 7\n  apiType: \"internal\"\n  category: \"social\"\n---\n\n# Linkedin API\n\n> Reverse-engineered internal API. Unofficial — may change without notice.\n\n## Documentation Index\n- `SKILL.md` (this file)\n- `references/REFERENCE.md` (detailed endpoint docs)\n- `references/ENDPOINTS.json` (machine-readable endpoint catalog)\n- `scripts/api.ts` (typed client interface)\n\n## Authentication\nSession Token (csrf-token) — Authentication method detected from captured traffic.\n\n### Providing credentials\n- Prefer passing auth as request headers or cookies at call time (do not hardcode secrets into the skill).\n- If executing via an external proxy/executor, pass per-call credentials (cookies and/or headers) so they are not persisted.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Runtime capable of HTTPS requests.\n- If using `scripts/api.ts`: TypeScript toolchain (or transpile to JS).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n### Data Read (1)\n- `GET /litms/api/metadata/user` — Get metadata about the current LinkedIn user.\n\n### Media (4)\n- `GET /dms/image/v2/{id}/{id}/{id}/{company-logo_100_100Id}/{timestamp}/{id}` — Retrieve a company logo image from LinkedIn.\n- `GET /dms/image/v2/{v2Id}/{id}/{id}/{b56zcyexl9hoaw-Id}/{timestamp}` — Retrieve a generic image from LinkedIn's DMS.\n- `HEAD /dms/image/v2/{id}/{id}/{id}/{company-logo_100_100Id}/{timestamp}/{id}` — Check if a company logo image exists on LinkedIn.\n- `HEAD /dms/image/v2/{id}/{id}/{id}/{profile-displayphoto-shrink_400_400Id}/{timestamp}` — Check if a user profile image exists on LinkedIn.\n\n### Core API (2)\n- `POST /{id}/api/{id}/{id}` — Post data to a specific LinkedIn API endpoint.\n- `POST /api/v2/msft` — Post data to a Microsoft-related LinkedIn API.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### OpenClaw (Unbrowse) workflow\n- Authenticate in the browser first (no credentials are shipped with this skill).\n- Capture fresh auth locally: run `unbrowse_capture` on an authenticated page for this domain.\n- Execute via backend gate + client browser executor: `unbrowse_replay` with `executionMode=\"backend\"`.\n\nExample:\n```text\nunbrowse_replay { service: \"linkedin\", executionMode: \"backend\", endpoint: \"GET /litms/api/metadata/user\" }\n```\n\nHere's the Quick Start content for the LinkedIn API skill document:\n\n```typescript\n// Get metadata about the current LinkedIn user.\nasync function getUserMetadata() {\n  const metadata = await client.getLitmsApiMetadataUser();\n  console.log(\"User Metadata:\", metadata);\n  return metadata;\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\n// Post data to a specific LinkedIn API endpoint (example: updating a user profile).\nasync function updateProfile(profileData: any, id: string) {\n  const response = await client.postApiV2Msft(profileData);\n  console.log(\"Profile Update Response:\", response);\n  return response;\n}\n```\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n**Type:** Reverse-engineered internal API (unofficial)\n**Auth:** Session Token (csrf-token)\n**Base URL:** `https://www.linkedin.com`\n**Captured Auth:** 2 auth headers, 19 session cookies\n\n## About This Skill\n\nThis skill provides access to Linkedin's internal API — the hidden endpoints that power their web/mobile app.\nThese are NOT official public APIs. They were captured by observing network traffic while using the site.\n\n**Important:**\n- Auth tokens in `auth.json` may expire — re-capture if you get 401 errors\n- Internal APIs can change without notice — endpoints may break\n- Rate limits are unknown — be conservative with request frequency\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\nUse this skill when you need to:\n- Access Linkedin data without official API access\n- Automate actions on www.linkedin.com (faster than browser automation)\n- Call the same endpoints the Linkedin frontend uses\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```typescript\nimport { LinkedinClient } from \"./scripts/api.ts\";\n\n// Load captured auth from auth.json\nconst client = await LinkedinClient.fromAuthFile(\"auth.json\");\n\n// Make requests to internal endpoints\nconst result = await client.get(\"/endpoint\");\n```\n\n## Captured Authentication\n\nThe `auth.json` file contains credentials extracted from browser traffic:\n- **Auth headers:** 2 (sec-fetch-storage-access, csrf-token)\n- **Session cookies:** 19\n\nIf auth expires, re-run `unbrowse_login` or `unbrowse_capture` to refresh tokens.\n\n## Internal Endpoints (11)\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\ntry {\n  const data = await client.get(\"/resource\");\n} catch (err) {\n  if (err.message.includes(\"401\")) {\n    // Auth expired — need to re-capture\n    console.error(\"Auth expired, re-run unbrowse_login\");\n  } else {\n    console.error(\"API error:\", err.message);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSee [REFERENCE.md](references/REFERENCE.md) for detailed endpoint documentation.\n"
